---
title: 2 Ingredient Donut Holes
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vzKuobmi3iI
servings: 8
---

== Donuts ==

Create self-rising flour by combining @flour{1%cup} with @baking powder{1.5%tsp}(alternatively, use .5 tsp baking soda). Combine with @yogurt{190%g}(plain, can substitute with 112g/half cup of milk). For a little more flavor add @?cinnamon{1%tbsp}.

Preheat @oil{} in your #pan{} to around 325°F. 

Put dough in a ziplock bag and cut the corner to create a pipet. Squeeze a little dough out and then slice with your scissors to create easy donut holes. Due to no yeast, they will drop to the bottom at first, but after a while they should float. Use a slotted spoon or spatula to move them around constantly, until they are golden. Then remove from oil and let rest on a paper towel.

== Toppings ==

For simple sugar coated donuts, simply toss in @?sugar{}.

For a glaze, mix @powdered sugar{2%cups}, @butter{2/3%stick}(melted), @vanilla{1%tsp}, and @milk{3%tbsp}(add another tbsp if you like thin glaze). To make this a chocolate glaze, add @?melted chocolate or cocoa powder{}(to taste).